Overlay patch 0023: iOS settings section (reference 0017 shape adapted to
SpaghettiKart's PortMenu) + game-side consumers for two of its knobs.

- PortMenu.cpp: "iOS" sidebar in Settings — Touch Controls (Hold to Lock
  A & Z per the MK64 policy, Haptics, Opacity, Left-Handed, Stick
  Response, Customize Layout…), Display (Max Frame Rate 60/120,
  Performance HUD), Menu (Menu Scale LIVE), Advanced (Remote Console
  :8768). Shell consumes the touch knobs via its 0.25 s poll (inherited
  with the Ship of Harkinian port shell); the two game-side consumers ride here:
- Engine.cpp GetInterpolationFPS: gSohIos.MaxFps caps the match-refresh
  branch (60 = battery saver, 120 = full ProMotion).
- Menu.cpp: the per-frame `io.FontGlobalScale = uiScale` clobber (the
  reason boot-time font scale never held once the menu drew) multiplies
  in gSohIos.MenuScale on iOS — fonts are live every frame; the slider
  callback ratio-rescales style sizes so paddings track live too.
Kart deltas vs reference 0017: no RaceDisable in this menu framework
(dropped); lock knob is the HOLD variant (user policy).

